<h2>Indian coriander seed for export</h2>
<p>Coriander is grown at scale across Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh and Gujarat, and we supply machine-clean seed in commercial and premium purity grades — whole or with a low, specified split content — to spice traders and food manufacturers.</p>

<p>Harvest runs February-April. Well-dried coriander seed stores for many months without significant quality loss, which lets us supply from stock through the year rather than only around harvest.</p>

<h2>How should I specify coriander seed?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Purity grade.</strong> 97-98% minimum machine-clean suits most bulk orders. For tighter quality-control programmes, ask about premium sortex-clean at 99%+.</li>
  <li><strong>Whole vs. split content.</strong> Whole seed is standard; we hold split content to ≤3-5% for orders specified as whole-grade.</li>
  <li><strong>Volatile oil content.</strong> Drives aroma and flavour strength, typically 0.3-0.8% and season-dependent — confirmed per lot on the certificate of analysis.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which markets buy Indian coriander seed?</h2>
<p>Malaysia and the UAE are the top two destinations by value — together roughly 36% of the total — followed by the United States, Saudi Arabia and the UK. See the cited country breakdown below.</p>

